# SRG-APP-000845-WSR-000220  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, verify when users
# create or update passwords, that the passwords are not found on the list
# of commonly-used, expected, or compromised passwords in IA-5 (1) (a).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000845-WSR-000220
group:           V-264348
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004061
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Password changes made through Splunk Web are evaluated by the same
                 platform settings, so the web tier's share is the [splunk_auth] password
                 history the benchmark authority prescribes for this product in
                 SPLK-CL-000410: enablePasswordHistory makes the platform retain previously
                 used passwords and passwordHistoryCount sets how many are refused at the
                 change dialog. The composition rules also observed here are asserted under
                 SRG-APP-000870.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory in true|True|TRUE|t|1|yes
check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] passwordHistoryCount min 5
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] passwordHistoryCount https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Screening a new password against a list of commonly used, expected, or
                 compromised passwords - not offered by the product; carried by the
                 directory service or identity provider and the organization's policy.
external:        Where authentication is external (LDAP, SAML, ProxySSO), the password is
                 created and verified at that provider and Splunk Web never sees the
                 change.
external:        Checking a new password against a list of commonly used, expected or
                 compromised passwords, which Splunk has no setting for: the native
                 controls cover reuse through enablePasswordHistory and
                 passwordHistoryCount, not membership of an external list.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:554, :561; SPLK-CL-000410 check
                 and fix text
finding:         Password changes made through Splunk Web are not checked against
                 previously used passwords as the product STIG requires -
                 authentication.conf [splunk_auth] enablePasswordHistory is missing or
                 false, or passwordHistoryCount is 4 or less; this determination is from
                 the perspective of the application layer alone, screening against a deny
                 list being carried by the identity provider and the organization's policy.
